test(e2e): prove the trashed-project fix by doing it, and unambiguate the date

Adds a seventh section to the workspace gate. It trashes the fixture's project out from
under a live document, reloads, and requires the rail to say "in the trash", to offer a
Restore action, to clear the banner once restored, and for the project to reappear in
GET /api/projects. It also asserts the underlying condition still holds — that
GET /api/projects/:id serves a soft-deleted project with 200 and deleted_at set — so if
the API is ever fixed to 404 instead, this test fails loudly rather than passing vacuously
against a defence that is no longer needed. 84 -> 93 assertions.

Visual check of the new banner flagged the deletion date rendering as "8/11/2026", which
is Aug 11 or 8 Nov depending on locale. Both banners now render "Aug 11, 2026", matching
the format the form editor already uses for Prepared on.
